<overview>
<p>Mechanized tracked platoons move their infantry in armored personnel carriers fitted with tracks for reliable all-terrain performance. Tracked APCs handle mud, snow, rubble, and rough ground better than any wheeled or hover alternative, making these platoons the preferred mechanized infantry for operations where terrain is uncertain or hostile. They sacrifice road speed compared to wheeled formations but gain the ability to keep pace with armored vehicles across broken ground. The APCs provide meaningful ballistic protection during transit, though troops must still dismount to fight effectively.</p><p>Towing assault-class LB-X autocannon that can fire cluster rounds capable of shredding virtually any target, these field gun crews deliver the heaviest area-effect direct fire available to ground forces. Ballistic plate personal armor helps improve the chances of surviving close contact with opposing forces.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as common date for LBX20 field gun. Ballistic plate armor chosen for heavy close-contact potential. Full complement of long arms selected due to low field gun ammo.
</notes>

